---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PeakChart from '../components/PeakChart.astro';
import { energy, fmt, pct, source, peaks, energyTx, losses, forecast, latest } from '../lib/energy';

const d = energy.derived;
const s01 = source(latest.source_id)!;
const f2030 = forecast.find((f) => f.year === 2030)!;
const f2026 = forecast.find((f) => f.year === 2026)!;
const bt = (energy.forecast.backtest as any)[energy.forecast.model_key];
const f2030s = energy.forecast.sensitivity.find((f) => f.year === 2030)!;
const lossNow = losses[losses.length - 1];
const levers = [
  ['Gas supply', "Most of Ghana's power comes from thermal plants. When gas runs short, available capacity falls below what the plants are rated for."],
  ['Hydro levels', 'Akosombo, Bui and Kpong depend on rainfall. Dry years cut output and limit when plants can run.'],
  ['New capacity', 'Plants and solar projects add supply, but projects slip. The model will test on-time and delayed cases.'],
  ['Cooling and heat', 'Hotter evenings push air-conditioning load into the peak hours.'],
  ['Electric vehicles', 'A small load today. The tool will show how much it would take for charging to matter, and how timing changes that.'],
  ['Transmission and payments', 'Thin lines in some corridors and unpaid bills in the sector can cause cuts even when plants are available.'],
];
---
<Base title="Energy" active="energy">
  <section style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px">
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:center">
      <span class="eyebrow">Energy</span>
      <span class="pill">Provisional: plant capacity not yet verified</span>
    </div>
    <h1 style="margin:0;font-size:44px;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.02em;max-width:18ch;text-wrap:balance">Demand is growing faster than the capacity we can confirm.</h1>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:0;max-width:62ch;font-size:17px">Ghana's peak electricity demand reached a record {fmt(d.peak_latest)} MW in {d.peak_latest_year}. This page tracks where it stands, where it is heading, and what could change the picture.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Latest figures" class="tiles">
    <div class="card tile"><span class="eyebrow">{d.peak_latest_year} peak demand</span>
      <span class="big">{fmt(d.peak_latest)} <small>MW</small></span>
      <span class="sub">Record high, up {pct(d.peak_yoy_pct)} on {d.peak_latest_year - 1}</span></div>
    <div class="card tile"><span class="eyebrow">Growth since {d.peak_since_year}</span>
      <span class="big">+{pct(d.peak_growth_since_pct)}</span>
      <span class="sub">About {pct(d.peak_cagr_since_pct)} a year, compounded. {pct(d.peak_cagr_full_pct)} a year since {d.peak_first_year}.</span></div>
    <div class="card tile"><span class="eyebrow">Energy transmitted, {d.peak_latest_year}</span>
      <span class="big">{fmt(d.energy_latest)} <small>GWh</small></span>
      <span class="sub">Up {pct(d.energy_yoy_pct, 2)} on {d.peak_latest_year - 1}</span>
      {d.energy_latest_confidence === 'low' && <span class="sub" style="color:var(--warn);font-weight:600">Low confidence: the published total and the loss figures disagree. <a href="/data/#conflicts">Details</a></span>}</div>
    <div class="card tile"><span class="eyebrow">Reserve margin</span>
      <span class="big" style="font-size:26px;padding:6px 0">Not yet verified</span>
      <span class="sub" style="color:var(--warn);font-weight:600">Needs confirmed plant capacity. Shown once checked.</span></div>
  </section>

  <section style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;align-items:flex-start">
    <div class="card" style="flex:999 1 640px;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;padding:20px 22px">
      <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:21px">Peak demand: history and baseline projection</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:0;font-size:14px">If demand keeps growing the way it has, annual peak reaches about {fmt(f2026.p50)} MW in 2026 and {fmt(f2030.p50)} MW by 2030 (likely range {fmt(f2030.p10)} to {fmt(f2030.p90)} MW). This is a trend projection, not a prediction of any single year.</p>
      <PeakChart />
      <p class="src" style="margin:0">Actual: <a href="/data/#sources">{s01.name}, {s01.publisher}, p. {latest.page.split(',').pop()?.trim()}</a>. Projection: {energy.forecast.model_version}, constant-growth fit to {peaks.length} annual peaks ({peaks[0].year} to {latest.year}); shaded band is an {energy.forecast.interval}. Peaks before 2017 were held down by load shedding, so they show what was delivered, not what was wanted. A fit to only the steadier years since 2019 gives a lower path, about {fmt(f2030s.p50)} MW in 2030. The projection excludes new demand sources such as EV charging. Capacity is not drawn because it has not been verified. In past tests, forecasts of this kind were off by about {pct(bt.mape * 100)} on average, but there were only {bt.n} test cases.</p>
    </div>
    <aside style="flex:1 1 300px;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
      <div class="card" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px">
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:18px">Early-warning level</h2>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap" aria-label="Levels: Adequate, Tight, Shortfall. None selected.">
          <span class="lvl" style="color:#0b6a37;background:#e3f4ea">Adequate</span>
          <span class="lvl" style="color:#8a5200;background:#fbefd9">Tight</span>
          <span class="lvl" style="color:#a82a21;background:#fbe5e2">Shortfall</span>
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0;font-size:13.5px"><b>Not assessed.</b> A level needs verified capacity as well as demand. It will appear here once the capacity data is loaded.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px">
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:18px">Transmission losses</h2>
        <span class="big" style="font-size:30px">{fmt(lossNow.value, 2)}<small>%</small></span>
        <span class="sub">{lossNow.year}. The regulator's limit is 4.10%.</span>
      </div>
      <a class="card" href="/scenarios/" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--text);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--header)">Try it</span>
        <span class="big" style="font-weight:700;font-size:20px">When could demand pass supply?</span>
        <span class="muted" style="font-size:14px">Test your own capacity figure, new plants and electric-vehicle charging.</span>
      </a>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
    <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:24px">What changes the picture</h2>
    <div class="levers">
      {levers.map(([t, b]) => (<div class="card"><div style="font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px">{t}</div><div class="muted" style="font-size:14px">{b}</div></div>))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:20px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 32px;font-size:13.5px" class="muted">
    <div style="flex:1 1 320px"><b style="color:var(--text)">Sources.</b> {s01.name}, {s01.publisher}, pp. 11 and 25 to 26. Capacity, generation and fuel data from the Electricity Supply Plan, PURC fact sheets and the Energy Commission Outlook are being verified. <a href="/data/">See all sources</a>.</div>
    <div style="flex:1 1 320px"><b style="color:var(--text)">Method.</b> Every number carries its source, year and whether it is an actual or a forecast. Conflicting sources are shown side by side. <a href="/data/#methods">Read the method</a> or <a href="/data/energy.json">download the data</a>.</div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .tiles { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:14px; }
  .tile { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:2px; padding:16px 18px; }
  .tile .big { font-weight:700; font-size:34px; line-height:1.1; }
  .big small { font-family:"Public Sans",sans-serif; font-weight:500; font-size:15px; color:var(--muted); }
  .sub { font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); }
  .lvl { font-size:13px; font-weight:600; border-radius:999px; padding:3px 12px; opacity:.55; }
  .levers { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:14px; }
  @media (max-width:900px) { .tiles { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); } .levers { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  @media (max-width:480px) { .tiles { grid-template-columns:1fr; } h1 { font-size:32px !important; } }
</style>
